.TH KILL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
kill \- send a signal to processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.PP
.BI "int kill(pid_t " process ", int " signal ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a Linux signal to the process or processes selected by
.IR process .
A positive value selects that PID, zero selects the caller's process group,
\-1 selects all permitted processes except process 1, and a value less than
\-1 selects the process group whose ID is the negated value.
Signal zero sends no signal but performs existence and permission checks.
.B <signal.h>
defines Linux signal constants including
.BR SIGTERM ,
.BR SIGKILL ,
and
.BR SIGCHLD .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.BR EINVAL ,
.BR EPERM ,
and
.BR ESRCH .
.SH NOTES
When a group is selected, success means at least one signal was sent.
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (3crunch),
.BR getpid (3crunch),
.BR kill (2),
.BR signal (7)
